:: StoryInterface
<!--
	Story shell — a persistent left rail beside the centered reading column
	that holds the story's single #passages element. RAW HTML: SugarCube wraps
	this content in its own #story element (authoring another one here is fatal)
	and does not process macros, so the chrome is plain HTML wired to
	SugarCube's global UI APIs with onclick. SugarCube 2.37 requires exactly
	one #passages inside a custom StoryInterface — this is the story's one and
	only; every passage renders inside it.
-->
<div class="shell">
	<aside class="rail">
		<h1 class="rail-title">Cam Safety</h1>
		<nav class="rail-actions">
			<a href="#" title="Settings" onclick="UI.settings();return false;">Settings</a>
			<a href="#" title="Saves" onclick="UI.saves();return false;">Saves</a>
			<a href="#" title="Restart" onclick="UI.restart();return false;">Restart</a>
			<!-- Prev/next, disabled: remove the comment markers below to re-enable (one line) -->
			<!-- <a href="#" title="Previous passage" onclick="Engine.backward();return false;">‹ Prev</a> <a href="#" title="Next passage" onclick="Engine.forward();return false;">Next ›</a> -->
		</nav>
	</aside>
	<div class="main">
		<div id="passages"></div>
	</div>
</div>
